{"causes": ["The growth of Christian communities in major Roman cities necessitated the establishment of episcopal leadership for governance and spiritual guidance.", "The ongoing process of Christianization within the Roman Empire created a need for figures like bishops to solidify religious institutions.", "The early Church tradition of venerating deceased bishops as saints encouraged the posthumous recognition and cult of individuals like Agrippinus."], "effects": ["Agrippinus's episcopacy helped to establish and consolidate the early Christian community and ecclesiastical structure in Naples.", "His veneration as a patron saint provided a spiritual protector for Naples against calamities for centuries.", "The cult of Saint Agrippinus contributed to the rich tapestry of local sainthood traditions within southern Italy."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "early-christianity", "sourceName": "Early Christianity", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "agrippinus-of-naples", "targetName": "Agrippinus of Naples", "context": "The doctrines and organizational structures of Early Christianity directly shaped Agrippinus's role and responsibilities as a bishop in the late 3rd century CE."}, {"sourceSlug": "agrippinus-of-naples", "sourceName": "Agrippinus of Naples", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "naples", "targetName": "Naples", "context": "Agrippinus's entire historical significance is inextricably linked to his service as bishop and subsequent veneration within the city of Naples."}, {"sourceSlug": "diocletianic-persecution", "sourceName": "Diocletianic Persecution", "verb": "OCCURS_DURING", "targetSlug": "agrippinus-of-naples", "targetName": "Agrippinus of Naples", "context": "Although not a martyr, Agrippinus's episcopacy in Naples coincided with the heightened persecution of Christians under Emperor Diocletian around 303 CE."}, {"sourceSlug": "agrippinus-of-naples", "sourceName": "Agrippinus of Naples", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "christianity-in-naples",